  "guideContent": {
    "strategyOverview": "Witherbloom, the Balancer is a {6}{B}{G} 5/5 Flying/Deathtouch Elder Dragon with affinity for creatures on itself AND grants affinity for creatures to every instant and sorcery you cast. The deck couples a wide-creature engine (tokens, aristocrats, recursion creatures) with generic-heavy I/S payoffs that scale with board state. With 6+ creatures in play the commander recasts for {B}{G} or free, and every I/S spell — X-drains, mass interaction, mass reanimation, tutors — becomes near-free.\n\nThe aristocrats half (Viscera Seer, Carrion Feeder, Pawn of Ulamog, Pitiless Plunderer, Blood Artist, Zulaport Cutthroat, Witherbloom Apprentice, Grave Pact) converts creature deaths into card draw, drain, and treasure ramp. Token generators (Bitterblossom, Ophiomancer, Awakening Zone, Hidden Stockpile, Mycoloth, Tendershoot Dryad, Avenger of Zendikar, Sprout Swarm, Infestation Sage) replenish the board and keep affinity hot. Recursion (Bloodghast on every land drop, Eternal Witness, Reanimate via Grave Researcher, Living Death) makes wraths and removal asymmetric in our favor.\n\nPrepared-mechanic creatures provide free copies of key sorceries: Emeritus of Woe stamps out Demonic Tutor copies, Stensian Sanguinist generates Exsanguinate copies when an attacker connects, Grave Researcher produces Reanimate copies as our GY fills, and Leech Collector creates Bloodletting copies on each turn's first lifegain. Three adventure creatures (Murderous Rider/Swift End, Beanstalk Giant/Fertile Footsteps, Foulmire Knight/Profane Insight) staple removal, ramp, and draw to bodies that also boost affinity.\n\nWin conditions are two-fold: Exsanguinate / Torment of Hailfire X-drains (affinity-cheap on a wide board), and commander damage from Witherbloom himself (flying/deathtouch + Swiftfoot Boots; 3-4 hits closes). Mass interaction is asymmetric only: Sheoldred's Edict (each opponent sacs), In Garruk's Wake (only opponents' creatures and PWs), Plague Wind (only creatures we don't control). The deck is Bracket 3 fair-power: 2 Game Changers (Necropotence, Bolas's Citadel), 3 tutors (Diabolic Intent, Buried Alive, Emeritus of Woe), conservative manabase (no Cabal Coffers / Urborg / Nykthos / Yavimaya / Boseiju), no infinite combos."
  },
